wiretap-server (0.1.9) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * The daemon names itself to the gateway: [forward] daemon_id, the host's
    short name when absent. An id the gateway would refuse stops startup.
  * A serial line frames with the catalogue the gateway assigns it, pulled,
    checked against its SHA-1 and kept under the state directory, else the
    catalog file in /etc, else none. A new assignment takes effect without
    a restart, and the daemon reports to the gateway what each line uses.
  * Against a gateway older than 0.1.7 the daemon falls back to protocol v2
    and receives no assignments, unless the database takes raw serial.
  * No configuration change is needed; install and restart.

 -- Alex Ferrara <alex@wiredsquare.com>  Sat, 03 Oct 2026 15:37:51 +1000

wiretap-server (0.1.8) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * A serial device can capture raw, framed or both: capture = "raw" or
    "both" in its [[device]] table, and raw_database to send the raw chunks
    to a database of their own. Absent, capture is "framed", as before.
  * Raw chunks are forwarded over ingest protocol v3, so a device with raw
    capture needs a 0.1.8 or later gateway; a 0.1.7 gateway refuses the
    chunks. Every other database stays on v2.
  * The ingest listener relays raw serial from a pusher only when a device
    here sends raw chunks to the default database.
  * No configuration change is needed; install and restart.

 -- Alex Ferrara <alex@wiredsquare.com>  Sat, 03 Oct 2026 13:44:23 +1000

wiretap-server (0.1.7) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * The ingest listener takes protocol versions 2 and 3. A v3 client gets
    no catalogue assignments yet, and a batch holding a raw serial record
    is refused as malformed. The forwarder still sends v2, so this package
    works against a 0.1.6 or older gateway.
  * A GVRET transmit waits for room in the interface's send queue instead
    of being refused while it is full.
  * A forwarding key over 255 bytes now fails to connect, naming its length.
  * No configuration change is needed; install and restart.

 -- Alex Ferrara <alex@wiredsquare.com>  Sat, 03 Oct 2026 11:55:32 +1000

wiretap-server (0.1.6) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * A modbus-rtu line's catalogue is read for its RTU rules and name only,
    and the binary is about 290 KB smaller. Its other sections (frames,
    meta.version, endianness) are no longer checked at startup; a catalogue
    with an empty meta.name is now refused.
  * An extended CAN frame whose id falls in the Test Pattern range is no
    longer answered during a run.
  * No configuration change is needed; install and restart.

 -- Alex Ferrara <alex@wiredsquare.com>  Tue, 29 Sep 2026 18:30:37 +1000

wiretap-server (0.1.5) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * A batch the gateway refuses for its contents is kept in
    cache.dead-letter.db beside the disk cache, in the cache's own format,
    instead of being resent for ever and holding up everything behind it.
    Nothing is dropped: if that file cannot be written, the batch is cached
    and retried as before.
  * A batch sent in pieces that failed partway is no longer stored twice:
    only the pieces the gateway did not take are cached and resent.
  * An ACK for a batch other than the one sent is refused, and the batch is
    cached and retried.
  * A gateway whose database is not ready yet is logged as such (HELLO
    status 4), not as a bad database name.
  * A serial device's parity is read in any case ("Even" as well as "even").
  * No configuration change is needed; install and restart.

 -- Alex Ferrara <alex@wiredsquare.com>  Tue, 29 Sep 2026 14:53:24 +1000

wiretap-server (0.1.4) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * CAN and serial lines are read through wiretap-lib-rs. An unplugged CAN
    adapter is read again when it returns, without a restart, and a loss is
    logged once rather than every second.
  * The serial line is now opened exclusively: while the server holds it,
    a second reader such as a debugging `cat` gets EBUSY. Stop the service
    before reading the line by hand.
  * A modbus-rtu device may name a catalogue of its vendor codes; see the
    shipped sungrow-rs485.catalog.toml. Optional; nothing changes without it.
  * Every frame the server has read before a stop is archived, and a
    stop no longer logs a spurious `queue FULL: size=0`.
  * A GVRET transmit declaring more than 8 bytes is refused, not cut to 8.
  * No configuration change is needed; install and restart.

 -- Alex Ferrara <alex@wiredsquare.com>  Tue, 29 Sep 2026 09:24:45 +1000

wiretap-server (0.1.3) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * No change to the daemon. Republished alongside the gateway, which gains
    per-database events and schema v3, so the two halves stay on one version.
    A 0.1.2 daemon is served by a 0.1.3 gateway without complaint.

